total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.7.dev3.official [60fff00a6]\nNot in v4.7.dev2.official [778cf54da]\nReverted [76c5567626187536080f7df13cee8b7f4789688e] and bug was fixed\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev3 - macOS Sequoia (15.7.3) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M4 (Apple9) - Apple M4 (10 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n```\nWhile attempting to print an error, another error was printed:\nERROR: Element limit reached.\n   at: _allocate_rid (./core/templates/rid_owner.h:122)\nWhile attempting to print an error, another error was printed:\nERROR: Parameter \"mem\" is null.\n   at: initialize_rid (./core/templates/rid_owner.h:284)\n```\nThis error kept spamming the console ever since I updated to ``v4.7.dev3`` upon loading my large project with many classes. Eventually, the errors would cease, probably because it was finished loading. When I tried to access some UI in my project that uses ``RichTextLabel``s, the entire editor would crash. Also, there reached a point that whenever I opened a new page of the class reference, it wouldn't render correctly. And when closing Godot, it would become unresponsive. This error didn't appear in another project.\n\nI bisected the issue to [76c5567626187536080f7df13cee8b7f4789688e], so when I reverted it, it was fixed. I'm not sure why, but it explains the bug because the class reference uses ``RichTextLabel``s.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nLater on, through more searching, I realized the issue was instigated by the ``open_help`` key of the section ``ScriptEditor`` of ``.godot/.editor/editor_layout.cfg``. It was set to this:\n``[\"@GDScript\", \"@GlobalScope\", \"Animation\", \"AnimationLibrary\", \"AnimationMixer\", \"AnimationPlayer\", \"AnimationTree\", \"Array\", \"BaseMaterial3D\", \"Basis\", \"BitMap\", \"Camera2D\", \"CanvasItem\", \"CanvasItemMaterial\", \"CollisionObject3D\", \"Color\", \"Control\", \"FogMaterial\", \"GeometryInstance3D\", \"Gradient\", \"Image\", \"Input\", \"InputEvent\", \"InputEventMouseButton\", \"InputEventMouseMotion\", \"Light2D\", \"Material\", \"MethodTweener\", \"Node\", \"Node2D\", \"Object\", \"OptionButton\", \"PackedByteArray\", \"PackedDataContainer\", \"PackedFloat32Array\", \"PackedInt32Array\", \"ParticleProcessMaterial\", \"PhysicalSkyMaterial\", \"PhysicsMaterial\", \"PopupMenu\", \"ProceduralSkyMaterial\", \"PropertyTweener\", \"RandomNumberGenerator\", \"RefCounted\", \"Resource\", \"ResourceLoader\", \"Shader\", \"ShaderInclude\", \"ShaderMaterial\", \"Signal\", \"SpriteFrames\", \"StandardMaterial3D\", \"String\", \"Thread\", \"Tween\", \"Viewport\", \"VisualShader\", \"Window\"]``\n\nI don't know if this is specific to my system or not, so it would be useful for others to check.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26539008/MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118275/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused"